  "text" : "In PyTorch, the dataset's job is to hand back one sample,\nand the data loader's job is to call it n number of times and hand back a batch.\nThe data loader is a machine with four different stations,\nand every argument you pass is one of those stations.\nYour dataset sits at the front.\nAll it knows is how to go get one sample wherever that data lives.\nThe first station is the sampler.\nIt decides the order.\nShuffle equals true is a random sampler,\na random sequence of indices.\nSecond up is fetch.\nWorkers will call your dataset with those indices in parallel if you ask for them.\nThird is batching. It collects batch-sized samples.\nAnd fourth is collate. This is what packs them into one tensor shaped for the GPU.\nOut comes the batch and what goes into the forward pass."
}
